===========================================================
Observations (not FAIL)
===========================================================
A. TestLoadScenarioSettingsLeavesFixedDateScenarioAlone survives the
   settings.go:419 mutation (it PASSes with the resolve removed). That is
   correct and expected — it is a no-op/negative guard asserting a fixed-date
   plan is NOT advanced, so it cannot be killed by removing the advance. The
   other two shipped tests in the same file ARE killed. Noted so the record
   does not imply all three are mutation-killed.
B. settings.go:2247 (the scenario RENAME path) decodes a scenario file with a
   bare `json.Unmarshal` — bypassing normalizeLoadedWhatIfSettings, hence
   resolveCurrentMonth — and rewrites the file. This is anchor-consistent and
   not a defect: start_date is preserved unchanged, and the per-type
   UnmarshalJSON still converts any legacy year keys to month keys at the same
   *12 value, so no schedule moves. Flagged only as a surface a future task
   touching the decode contract must remember to enumerate.
C. Out of scope for RC2, already logged at attempt 1 and unchanged here: the
   inline edit inputs in expense-sources-list.html render
   `value="{{div .StartMonth 12}}"`, which for a non-aligned offset emits a
   float (e.g. value="0.9166666666666666") that parseFormInt rejects with 400
   on re-save. Criterion 7 pins this as the deliberate loud interim; RC3
   replaces those inputs.
